    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0466" n="1200" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1200"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dupuy de Lôme to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Swampscott
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-09-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I am informed that on the 17th instant at 8.30 p.m., by Pennsylvania Railroad, in
                    special car No. 5841, a consignment of arms and ammunition, comprising 450 boxes
                    ammunition, 20 boxes of rifles marked <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi> in a
                    diamond, has been sent to Charles Raymond, esq., Southport, N. C. These arms, I
                    am informed, are for the insurgents in Cuba, and will be shipped probably to
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Commodore</hi>, which left New London, Conn., a
                    few days ago. Will return to Washington as soon as my health will permit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dupuy de Lôme</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
